```php
// Using multiple split calls
$lines = "hello,world;foo,bar;baz,qux";
$linesArray = array();
foreach (explode("\n", $lines) as $line) {
    $lineArray = array();
    foreach (explode(";", $line) as $field) {
        $fieldArray = array();
        foreach (explode(",", $field) as $value) {
            $lineArray[] = $value;
        }
        $fieldArray[] = $lineArray;
        $lineArray = $fieldArray;
    }
    $linesArray[] = $lineArray;
}

// Using str_split
$linesArray = array();
foreach (explode("\n", $lines) as $line) {
    $lineArray = array();
    $lineArray = array_merge($lineArray, str_split($line, 1));
    $lineArray = array_merge($lineArray, str_split($line, 2));
    $lineArray = array_merge($lineArray, str_split($line, 3));
    $linesArray[] = $lineArray;
}
```
In the first example, we use multiple `explode` calls to split the input string into an array of values.
